# The engine's stall meter: while streams decode, the time between two decode rounds is time every one of them waits.
# It is measured on rank 0 inside the engine, because a client sees it only behind the stream smoothing, which hides
# pauses up to about 0.4 s. Each gap is broken down by what the scheduler did in between (admit; round: a prompt chunk
# or a spill write; finish; reply). /health's "stalls": the number of gaps, the worst, how many reached 50 ms, 100 ms,
# 250 ms, 500 ms and 1 s, and the last 32 of 50 ms or more, each with the wall time it ended and its parts,
# and the engine's own wall time ("now"), so a reader on another machine places each gap on its own clock.
# mgllm, 2026-10-08.
# Tests: tests/test_9008_stall_meter.py (CPU).

